{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Healthcare Data Governance Case Study\n","**Portfolio project: bridges the Data Analyst and AI Governance/Compliance tracks**\n","\n","## Background\n","Healthcare organizations constantly face a tradeoff: real patient data is the most useful for building and testing tools, but it carries real privacy risk and regulatory burden (HIPAA in the US, NDPR in Nigeria). One response to this is **synthetic data** a  realistic, computer-generated patient records that behave statistically like real data but aren't tied to any real person.\n","\n","This project uses **Synthea**, a real, open-source synthetic patient data generator built by MITRE, and asks a governance question instead of a \"find the pattern\" question.\n","\n","## Business question\n","**What does responsible data governance look like in healthcare, and how does synthetic patient data compare to real de-identified data as a governance strategy?**\n","\n","## The data\n","A small Synthea sample (e.g. ~1,000 synthetic patients), downloaded as CSV files from https://synthea.mitre.org/downloads fully synthetic, zero real people involved. Typical files: `patients.csv`, `conditions.csv`, `medications.csv`, `encounters.csv`.\n","\n","\n","Note: \"Project 1\" referenced below is the Hospital Readmission Risk\n","Analysis project in the same portfolio (real de-identified hospital\n","data). This project uses synthetic data instead, to evaluate it as\n","a governance strategy."],"metadata":{"id":"MV1_2KP9U1Y6"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 1. Setup\n"],"metadata":{"id":"JT7HmRyDaHGI"}},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"SZeeLhqMchwk","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1790436492744,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":117,"user":{"displayName":"Ayo","userId":"05827135324850076928"}},"outputId